A||||7||THE BEAST||4.9 vs. 3.4 vs. 3.8 SC Which one is best? ||||5||
Z||000000||THE BEAST||02-06-2001||05:33 PM||||I GUESS I HAVE MORE THAN ONE QUESTION ABOUT THE 4.9 CADDY. <BR>ONE IS WHAT ARE THE REAL SPECS ON THIS ENGINE (HP/TORQUE) AND THE “EXACT WEIGHT”? <P>AND  I ALSO READ THAT IT IS REALLY HARD TO GET THE IDLE SPEED TO BE SMOOTH (COMPUTER CONFLICTS). HAS ANY BODY BEEN ABLE TO CLEAR UP THIS PROBLEM  <P>  <BR>I NEED HELP -- I'M DEBATING BETWEEN GETTING A 3.4 PUSH ROD OR A 4.9 CADDY <BR>I WANT SOME GOOD POWER BUT I’M VERY CONCERNED ABOUT THE WEIGHT. <P>DOES ANYONE KNOW OF ANY GOOD SITES WITH INFO ABOUT THIS? <P>OR, DOES ANYONE KNOW ANYTHING ABOUT THE 3.8 SC ENGINE. LIKE INSTALLATION, IS THE EFFORT WORTH THE OUTCOME? HOW'S THE WEIGHT, HP, & TORQUE COMPARED TO THE 4.9 CADDY.<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||rockcrawl||02-06-2001||08:04 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>AND I ALSO READ THAT IT IS REALLY HARD TO GET THE IDLE SPEED TO BE SMOOTH (COMPUTER CONFLICTS). HAS ANY BODY BEEN ABLE TO CLEAR UP THIS PROBLEM<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Where did you read that?? It sounds like someone was either using the wrong ECM, or trying to run a heavilly modded engine with a stock ECM. I have a '91 Caddy 4.9 and I can't imagine a smoother running engine. I also have an '87 4100HT and it also runs (ran) very smooth. The 4100 is in my Ferrari replica, but I bought the 4.9 to replace it. I'm going to hang on to the 4.1 for use in a Fiero someday.<P>Cadillac's ratings are 135 hp/ 180 ftlb for the 4.1 and 200 hp/ 275 ftlb for the 4.9. I don't know the exact weight, but I'm told the 4.9 weighs within 10 lbs of a 2.8. <P>Any of the engines you are considering would be worthwhile, but the 4.9 will probably be the cheapest and the best power per dollar spap, and also the lightest.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||02-06-2001||11:11 PM||||Is that 4.9 and iron block with iron heads?<P>I find it difficult that there would only be 10 lbs of material to make up for 2 more cylinders, plus all of the fabrication brackets. But stranger things have been known to happen.<P>But I am curious about why someone would go to a V8 and not go 5.7. Even with aluminum heads an 88GT V8 weighed in at 2910 and had 330 hp. If one is going through a V8 why pick a Cadillac? Availability?<P>Im just wondering why someone would choose one over the other. Unless it was just by chance of the Automotive Gods to obtain a Caddie engine for cheap. <P>Here in California, the 3.4 would be the way to go to escape the mean ol' smog man. Trying to get a V8 through smog just blows away the typical smog schmuck used to dealing with Cavaliers and Hondas.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||02-07-2001||12:29 AM||||Engine swaps are easy in California. You just need to get a BAR sticker and the smog folks leave you alone.||||reg||5
Z||000004||lou_dias||02-07-2001||08:19 AM||||The 4.9 is an alumninum engine.<BR>That's why it weighs the same as the iron 2.8<BR>and I believe the hp is 215 not 200.  I also find it hard to beleive that the 4.1 Caddy v8 only made 135 hp...||||reg||1
Z||000005||BUCK WILLIAMS||02-07-2001||11:09 AM||||IS THERE ANY MODIFICATIONS OTHER THAN RADICAL CAMS THAT WOULD PUMP A LITTLE MORE HP OUT OF THE 4.9 AND STILL RUN SMOOTH AND BE RELIABLE IN A FIERO?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Will||02-07-2001||11:18 AM||||A while back someone posted the website of an outfit that swapped 4.9's into W(?)bodies. He claimed to be able to rebuild them for 280 HP. With a hybrid distributor you could use programmable LT1 electronics and avoid any ECM difficulties there might be.<P>Cadillac engines are very well engineered and usually lighter than other engines of comparable displacement. The Caddy 500 my father and I just put into our suburban is significantly lighter than the 454 that came out.<P>WKDFIERO:<P>Whiel 2910 my not be very heavy, it is still &gt;100 lbs heavier than a 4.9, N*, or 3.4 Fiero would be. What's your weight ditribution? How does your car handle with the extra rear weight bias, and what have you done to your suspension?<BR>4.9 engines can also be found very cheap. A junkyard I will visit this weekend has one with 70K miles for ~$500.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Will||02-07-2001||04:48 PM||||This thread:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008310.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008310.html</A> <P>Brings up the website I mentioned about performance rebuilds for 4.9||||reg||1
